    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d246">

                <pb facs="0684" n="654" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v08/pg654"/>

                <head>246. Letter From Secretary of Commerce Hodges to President Johnson<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d246-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1964-08-10">August 10, 1964</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Dear Mr. President:</p>
                <p>Following your instructions to seek additional funds for the commercial
                    specialist program of the Foreign Service, Secretary Rusk and I have personally
                    appealed to the Senate Appropriations Committee for the addition of one million
                    dollars to State’s budget. The fact that State earlier claimed no increase in
                    its personnel makes it desirable that you call Senator McClellan to indicate
                    your approval of this change in State’s budget. Deputy Under Secretary Crockett
                    of State and Tom Wyman of my staff have detailed the request to the Senator this
                    week, justifying the specific needs and the posts to which the new officers
                    would be assigned.</p>
                <p>For your use, the $1 million would permit assigning 37 new U.S. officers overseas
                    in addition to the existing 149; 15 of the 37 officers would be assigned to
                    posts where there are no commercial officers; we would also add 100 local and 8
                    U.S. clerical assistants. As you know, without these new officers our successful
                    export drive simply cannot be sustained.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Luther H. Hodges</hi>
                        <anchor n="2" xml:id="d246-f2"/>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>P.S. The Senate Subcommittee mark-up of the State Department appeal will
                        start today.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d246-f3"/>
                    </p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d246-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d246-f1-content">
